I like to carry two (oilskin) sacks and two BoH.  One sack holds
lightweight stuff that's too valuable to risk in a BoH explosion or to
theft/destruction: wands of death/polymorph/wishing, scrolls of
charging/taming/teleportation, a spare potion of holy water, some
food, rings of whatever, etc.  Having caused one too many explosions,
I keep nothing in this sack that cannot be put in a BoH, such as a
wand of cancellation.

Another sack I use as a shell for the BoH which carries a bunch of
useful stuff like food, more potions of holy water, extra AoLS,
wands/horns, a magic whistle and some leashes, etc.  This sack I drop
if I need to lose some weight, though by the time I'm venturing down
into hell, I usually only bother for demon lords and the like.
Earlier in the game, I'm often traveling lightly enough to be
unburdened.

I also carry another BoH out in the open, just so that I can collect
gems, gold, potions, and other random stuff without bothering to take
the main BoH out of its sack.  It is also handy to have a second BoH
when I want to transfer a bunch of stuff from one cache to another,
since I don't have to dig through the stuff I'm transferring to get to
the stuff I need while I'm traveling.  Also, sometimes I'm moving so
much stuff around I can't take both BoH up a flight of stairs at the
same time.

As you might have guessed, I tend to accumulate lots of stuff,
especially since I'm an avid polypiler ("Cool!  A cursed ring of
hunger, a bugle, and yet another spellbook of cure blindness!  More
stuff for the polypile!" :-)

